===Etymology 2===
{{etydate|1425}}, in {{w|Middle English}}; from {{inh|en|enm|intoxicat|intoxicat(e)|t=(''of a weapon or drug'') smeared, anointed or filled with poison; (''of a human being, animal'') poisoned, intoxicated|pos=also used as the past participle of {{m|enm|intoxicaten}}}}, see {{af|en|-ate|id1=adjective|pos1=adjective-forming suffix}} and [[#Etymology 1|Etymology 1]] for more. The {{glossary|noun}} was derived by {{glossary|substantivization}} from the {{glossary|adjective}}, see {{af|en|-ate|id1=substantive|pos1=noun-forming suffix}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈtɒksɪkət/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈtɑksɪkət/|a=GA}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}} {{tlb|en|obsolete}}

# [[inebriated|Inebriated]], [[intoxicated]].
#: {{syn|en|chemically inconvenienced|Thesaurus:drunk}}
# [[overexcited|Overexcited]], as with joy or grief.
#: {{syn|en|fever-pitched|highwrought|Thesaurus:enthusiastic}}
#* {{RQ:Chapman Eastward Hoe|passage=Alas, good mother, be not '''intoxicate''' for me; / I am well enough.}}
# {{lb|en|of a weapon or drug}} [[empoisoned|Empoisoned]], [[smeared]] with [[poison]], [[rendered]] poisonous.
# [[killed|Killed]] by [[poison]].
# {{lb|en|of a disease}} [[caused|Caused]] by [[poison]].

====Noun====
{{en-noun}} {{tlb|en|obsolete}}

# One who is [[intoxicated]].

